--- answer ---
The bug: on a non-matching item, the cached (matching) items are yielded but the cache is never cleared, so they get yielded again at the next non-matching item.Cause: in `rstrip` (more_itertools/more.py:2650-2655), matching items were cached but `cache` was never cleared after being yielded, so interior matching items (e.g. the `None` in `[None, 1, None, 2]`) were yielded again at each subsequent non-matching item.

Fix: added `cache_clear()` after `yield from cache` so each yielded run of matching items is emptied from the cache.

Note: the sandbox denied all python/compileall runs, so I couldn't execute the verification — the fix is unverified by a run; the docstring example (`[None, False, None, 1, 2, None, 3]`) and interior-match cases now follow from the code by inspection.